fix(tool-market): a trend has a side, and the judge must check it

Back-testing our own judge_setup against his published posts (163, 2026-11-13)
exposed a hole: it approved a LONG at the top of an oversold bounce in gold while
-DI 30.4 dominated +DI 15.4 at ADX 25.5. It passed because the only direction check
was the four-colour regime gate, which fires ONLY when stochastic sits inside an
extreme band — that day Stoch was 20.96, one point above it.

So the gate silently depended on an oscillator threshold sitting in the right place.
Rereading the two later posts (11-16, 11-17) the same proposal was vetoed, purely
because Stoch had fallen to 8.3 — the tool's verdict was decided by an accident of
where the oscillator rested, not by the trend.

New gate 'trend-side': when ADX >= 20 a trend exists, and +DI/-DI name its side, so
a proposal against the dominant DI is vetoed outright. Below ADX 20 there is no side
to be against and the gate stands aside, leaving range trades to the regime gate.

Regression: gold 2026-11-13 long @4136 now returns STAND ASIDE (was ACT), matching
his own call that day ('not an uptrend yet, at most an oversold bounce'). All three
article dates now agree with him.

Also adds the test the suite was missing: proof that the tool can return ACT at all.
Without it, a judge that only ever refuses looks rigorous while being broken.

35 test files, 559 tests.